-- ============================================================
-- Alonecraft 4.61 -- Rogue / Subtlety
--   Preparation -> Bladework
--   Dirty Deeds -> also cheapens Bladework
-- ============================================================
--
-- TODO.md:
--   "Preparation (Renamed to Bladework): Redesigned. AOE combo point
--    spender, 60 energy. Nearby enemies are marked for rapid counterattack,
--    causing their next three attacks on you to be immediately countered
--    for 125% weapon damage (180% if a dagger is equipped). 30s debuff
--    duration."
--   "Dirty Deeds: Also reduces the energy cost of Bladework."
--
--
-- BLADEWORK (14185, was Preparation)
--
--   The talent slot (284) is reused rather than moved, so Premeditation's
--   prerequisite on it is untouched and Talent.dbc needs no edit.
--
--   Effect1 becomes SPELL_EFFECT_DUMMY aimed at TARGET_UNIT_SRC_AREA_ENEMY
--   (15) with radius index 13 (10 yards); RogueBladework.cpp puts the mark
--   on each unit it hits.
--
--     RecoveryTime  480000 -> 0     it is an energy and combo point cost
--                                   now, not a long-cooldown button
--     PowerType     0 -> 3          energy
--     ManaCost      0 -> 60
--     AttributesEx  32 -> 1048608   adds SPELL_ATTR1_FINISHING_MOVE_DAMAGE
--                                   (0x00100000), which is what makes
--                                   SpellInfo::NeedsComboPoints (:1298)
--                                   true and gets the points consumed
--
--   SpellFamilyFlags1 keeps bit 12 (4096), Preparation's own unique rogue
--   family bit -- that is how Dirty Deeds finds it below, and no new flag
--   had to be invented.
--
--
-- THE TWO NEW SPELLS
--
--   200504  Marked for Counterattack   30 s debuff on the enemy, 3 charges
--   200505  Counterattack              125% weapon damage
--
--   The mark sits on the ENEMY and fires when the enemy attacks, which is
--   the same shape as Mark of Blood (MarkOfBloodRework.cpp:24): inside the
--   proc, eventInfo.GetActor() is the enemy and GetActionTarget() is the
--   rogue, so the counterattack is cast from the rogue at the enemy.
--
--   Charge limiting is the spell_proc row's Charges = 3, not ProcCharges
--   guesswork -- and SpellPhaseMask is 2.  A spell_proc row with
--   SpellPhaseMask 0 never fires and gives no error.
--
--   ProcFlags 20 = PROC_FLAG_DONE_MELEE_AUTO_ATTACK (0x4) |
--   PROC_FLAG_DONE_SPELL_MELEE_DMG_CLASS (0x10), so both swings and melee
--   abilities count as "their next three attacks".
--
--   200505 deliberately carries SpellFamilyName 0.  SpellEffects.cpp:3422
--   hands +50% dagger damage to anything in the rogue family matching
--   0x6000000, and inheriting that would collide with the 180% the spec
--   asks for.  With no family, the script owns the dagger branch outright.
--
--
-- DIRTY DEEDS (14082, 14083)
--
--   Effect1 is already ADD_FLAT_MODIFIER / EffectMiscValue 14
--   (SPELLMOD_COST).  Its word A (1280 = Cheap Shot + Garrote) is kept and
--   Bladework is added in word B.
--
--   CLASS-MASK COLUMN TRAP: effect 1's word B is the column named
--   EffectSpellClassMaskA2, not B1.  Getting this wrong silently masks
--   nothing.
--
-- ============================================================


